Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
How fast does photon loss erase the Heisenberg advantage of a NOON state?\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To measure an optical phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 ", we send light through the arm that carries it and read the phase off the \
output. The precision of that reading is set by the state we send in. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " independent photons, each an independent estimate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 ", the error averages down as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 ": this is the shot-noise limit. A NOON state, the two-mode superposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", "0"}]},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
         StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " of all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " photons in one arm or all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " in the other, does better. Because the two branches accumulate phase at \
opposite ends, the superposition winds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " times faster than a single photon, and the error falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ": the Heisenberg limit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The figure of merit behind both scalings is the quantum Fisher information ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 ": the Cramer-Rao bound says the error of any unbiased estimator of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " for one shot. Shot noise is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 "; the NOON state reaches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ". The quadratic gain is the whole point of the state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That gain is also fragile. A NOON state is a maximally delocalized \
superposition, and losing even one of its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " photons tells the environment which arm the light was in, which is exactly \
the information the interferometer was hiding. So the question of this essay \
is: ",
 StyleBox["as photons leak out of the interferometer, how fast does the \
Fisher information fall, and when does the Heisenberg advantage drop below \
plain shot noise?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The answer, computed below, is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " the per-photon transmission: the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 " sensitivity survives only on the branch where every photon makes it \
through, and that branch has weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["\<\
The lossless half of this story is the representation worked out in Chapter 6 \
(SU(2) interferometry in the joint Fock-polarization basis) and Chapter 3 \
(the two-mode NOON state and its Wigner function). The lossy half is the \
extension.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell["\<\
Load the checked-out QF paclet, then its main and bosonic constructors:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"PacletDirectoryLoad", 
  "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework/\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell["Load the main context:", "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Expose the second-quantization context, which carries ",
 Cell[BoxData["AnnihilationOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " and the Fock constructors:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The NOON state and its Fisher information: a two-mode cat that winds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " times faster"
}], "Section",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We work with two bosonic modes, the two arms of the interferometer. A NOON \
state of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 " puts all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " photons in the first arm or all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " in the second, in equal superposition. Since loss can only lower the \
photon number and no arm ever holds more than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", a Fock cutoff of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " levels per mode holds every state we will meet: the truncation is exact \
here, not an approximation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the NOON state as a vector in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " two-mode space, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", "0"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " the two populated basis kets:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"noonState", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"d", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", " ", "d"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"d", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2.", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look at the order-two state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", ",", "0"}]},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "2"}]},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"noonState", "[", "2", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell["Confirm it is a legitimate normalized state:", "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"noonState", "[", "2", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The phase is imprinted on one arm: a phase shift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 " on the second mode acts by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ", so the generator of the estimation is the number operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2", "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " of that mode. Build it on the two-mode space. The identity on the \
untouched mode is written with an explicit dimension, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "d", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}], ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 ", so the two-mode tensor product never has to guess a cutoff:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"numberTwo", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a2", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "d", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
      "        ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"a2", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "a2"}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a pure state the quantum Fisher information is four times the variance \
of the generator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", "4", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2", "2"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 ": this is exactly the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["Var",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " of the SU(2) treatment in Chapter 6, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " here specialized to the single-arm number operator. Take expectations by \
tracing the operator against the density matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"expval", "[", 
   RowBox[{"op_", ",", " ", "qs_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Re", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"op", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"qs", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the pure-state Fisher information and evaluate it across ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"pureQFI", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"numberTwo", "[", "n", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"qs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"noonState", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"4", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"expval", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"g", " ", "@", " ", "g"}], ",", " ", "qs"}], "]"}], " ", "-",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"expval", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "qs"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " for the first several NOON orders:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Chop", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"pureQFI", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " exactly: the two branches are eigenstates of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " with eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 ", so the variance is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " and four times it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ". The sensitivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"]], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " is the Heisenberg limit, a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " below the shot-noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " independent photons. This is the lossless advantage we now expose to \
loss."
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell["\<\
Photon loss as a Lindblad channel: evolving each arm toward vacuum\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Loss is each arm leaking photons into an unwatched environment. For a mode \
with annihilation operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 ", pure loss is the Lindblad equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "."], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "}"}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 ", under which the mean photon number decays as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 ". So a channel of transmission ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 ", meaning each photon survives with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 ", is loss at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " run for a time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["log",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 ". In other words, we do not need a separate loss parameter: the \
transmission ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " fixes the evolution time."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 " takes the generator, the jump operators with their rates, the initial \
state, and the time: with a zero Hamiltonian and unit rate on each arm's \
annihilation operator, evolving to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["log",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " applies transmission ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 " to both modes. Build the annihilation operators on the two-mode space with \
the same explicit-dimension identity, and return the lossy density matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lossyNOON", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "eta_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\n", "        ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"a1", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", 
            RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "d", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}], ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        "\n", "        ", 
        RowBox[{"a2", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "d", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", 
            RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "\n", "        ", 
       "}"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
      RowBox[{"With", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"evolution", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"0.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"a1", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
               "a1"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"a1", ",", " ", "a2"}], "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
            "                ", 
            RowBox[{"noonState", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", 
               RowBox[{"Log", "[", "eta", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
        ",", "\n", "            ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"evolution", " ", "/.", " ", 
           RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", 
             RowBox[{"Log", "[", "eta", "]"}]}]}]}], ")"}], 
         "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Loss turns the pure NOON state into a mixture. Check that the order-two \
state at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " is no longer pure: its purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 " drops below one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lossyNOON", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0.9"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell["\<\
As expected, the purity is below one: a fraction of the population has fallen \
out of the two-photon NOON manifold into states with a missing photon, which \
carry which-arm information and cannot interfere.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Fisher information under loss: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"]
}], "Section",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a mixed state the Fisher information is no longer four times a \
variance. The general form sums over the eigenpairs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], ",", 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]}],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "-", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftBracketingBar]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          TemplateBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"]},
           "Bra"], 
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["G", "TI"], "^"], 
          TemplateBox[{
            StyleBox["j", "TI"]},
           "Ket"]}], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["|",
           SpanMaxSize->1], "2"]}], ","}]}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 " the phase generator and the sum restricted to pairs with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 ". In words, only coherences between eigenstates of different population \
contribute, weighted by how distinguishable the two populations are. \
Implement it, symmetrizing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 " to exactly Hermitian first so the eigensolver returns real eigenvalues:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qfi", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho_", ",", " ", "g_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"l", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "m"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"l", ",", " ", "v"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Eigensystem", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"rho", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "rho", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
        "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"l", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "[", "l", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "v", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "g", " ", ".", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "v", "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Flatten", " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "        ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"l", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"l", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", ">", " ", "1*^-12"}], ",",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"l", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"l", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"l", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"l", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
               RowBox[{"m", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", 
              "2"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "l", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "l", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compare the computed Fisher information with the closed form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 ", for NOON orders up to ten:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"qfi", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"lossyNOON", "[", 
           RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "0.9"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"numberTwo", "[", "n", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}],
           "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"0.9", "^", "n"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   "    ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "10", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the two columns agree to six or seven digits: the Fisher \
information of the lossy NOON state is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 ". The mechanism is clean. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 " sensitivity lives entirely on the coherence between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", "0"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 ", the only pair whose populations differ by the full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ". That coherence survives only when all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 " photons are transmitted, an event of probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 ". Every term in which a photon is lost maps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", "0"}]},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1", ",", "0"}]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 ", a state orthogonal to anything the other branch collapses to, so it is \
which-arm information and carries no phase sensitivity at all. The surviving \
coherence keeps its full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 ", scaled by its weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Check the lossless limit as a consistency test: at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " the evolution time is zero and the Fisher information must return to the \
pure-state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qfi", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Normal", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lossyNOON", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"numberTwo", "[", "n", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " is recovered: with nothing lost, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " and the mixed-state formula reduces to the pure-state result."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "When the advantage collapses: loss turns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 " into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"]
}], "Section",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Having checked ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 " against QF, we can read the sensitivity straight off the closed form. The \
lossy NOON error is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ", to be set against the lossless Heisenberg ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 " and the shot-noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 ". Define the three sensitivities:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sensitivities", "[", "eta_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<NOON, lossless\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "n"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<shot noise\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "n", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<NOON, loss \>\"", " ", "<>", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ToString", "[", "eta", "]"}]}], " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"eta", "^", "n"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " the factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 " shrinks faster than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " grows, so the lossy NOON error stops falling, turns around, and eventually \
climbs past the shot-noise line. Solve for the photon number where the lossy \
NOON Fisher information drops back to shot noise, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"n", " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FindRoot", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"n", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0.9", "^", "n"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "30"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 " the crossover sits near this photon number: below it the NOON state still \
beats independent photons, above it the surviving coherence is too rare to \
pay for the delocalization, and more photons make the estimate worse. Plot \
the three sensitivities on a log scale to see the lossy curve bottom out and \
cross:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", "\n", "    ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sensitivities", "[", "0.9", "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "40", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"First", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"sensitivities", "[", "0.9", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   "    ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<photon number n\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[Delta]\[Theta] = 1/\!\(\*SqrtBox[\(F\)]\)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Phase sensitivity: loss turns the Heisenberg curve \
around\>\""}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "560"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The lossless NOON line falls as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " forever, always below shot noise; the lossy line tracks it at small ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ", reaches a minimum near the photon number where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " peaks, and then rises through the shot-noise line at the crossover just \
computed. The Heisenberg scaling is not merely degraded by loss, it is \
reversed: past the optimum, adding photons to a lossy NOON state costs \
precision rather than buying it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the qualitative reason NOON states are not how large-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 " optical metrology is actually done. The loss-limited bound of ",
 ButtonBox["Demkowicz-Dobrzanski et al.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.3940"], None}],
 " says the best achievable error under transmission ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 " scales as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[GreaterTilde]", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "N"}], "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 ", a shot-noise-like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 " with a loss-dependent prefactor; coherent-plus-squeezed light approaches \
it, while the NOON state, with its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 " cliff, falls short for all but the smallest ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell["The answer", "Section",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The quantum Fisher information of a NOON state of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " in the ideal case and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 " under per-photon transmission ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 ", a result the mixed-state Fisher-information formula confirms against the \
closed form to six digits for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 " up to ten. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " factor is the sensitivity of the single coherence between the two extremal \
Fock states; the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " factor is the probability that this coherence survives, since every lost \
photon is a which-arm witness that kills it. For any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "<", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " the product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],
 " rises, peaks, and falls, so the phase error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 " has a minimum at a finite ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " and climbs back through the shot-noise line beyond it. The Heisenberg \
advantage is real only while the whole state stays intact, and photon loss \
makes that a small-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " luxury."
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"
]
